{
  "original_id": "primary-20260913-multiset-rook",
  "archive_id": "BW2-PR20260913-multiset_rook",
  "title": "A counterexample to multiset rook-Eulerian interlacing",
  "batch_label": "primary",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "disproved",
  "scope": "Under Definitions 5, 8, 9 and equations (10)--(12) of Alexandersson--Jal--Quemener, arXiv:2502.05939v1, take the non-skew Ferrers board lambda=(3,3,3,3,4,4) and content alpha=(2,2,1,1). There are exactly 60 legal words with strict adjacent ascents and no sentinel, and the first-entry refinements are R3=t(t^2+8t+3), R2=t(8t^2+15t+1), and R1=t^2(t+7)(2t+1). The sequence (R3,R2,R1) is not interlacing: its required ordered pair R3 preceq R1 fails because their degrees are 3 and 4 and minroot(R3)=-4-sqrt(13)<-7=minroot(R1). Thus the interlacing clause of Conjecture 28 is false, disproving the exact original conjunction frozen in source.md. This does not decide the separately quantified total real-rootedness clause. Indeed, all three refinements and the total R=2t(t^3+12t^2+15t+2) in this witness are real-rooted. No minimality or universal total-polynomial counterexample is asserted.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
